{Name: Sweatheart / Gender: Female / Appearance: Sweetheart is a flamboyant and commanding figure styled in an exaggerated, over-the-top magical girl aesthetic. Her entire design is drenched in shades of pink and red, emphasizing her obsession with love and herself. She has long, voluminous pink hair tied into twin-tails with a large polka-dotted bow perched on top of her head, reinforcing her overly cutesy appearance. Her dress is a classic ballgown style with a poofy skirt and frilly, scalloped hem lined with lace. It features a white ruffled collar and puffed sleeves. She has a light pink headband that has a cracked reddish-pink heart symbol on it. Despite the girlishness of her outfit, she exudes arrogance and intensity, which contrasts humorously with her sugary design. in combat, Sweetheart wields a heart-themed flail-like scepter: a pink rod topped with a faceted gem and ending in a spiked, strawberry-shaped ball suspended by a chain, hinting at her aggressive tendencies beneath the sweet exterior. It is not possible to see due to her clothes, but part of her canonical design is a literal hole in her abdomen, similar to a donut. / Personality: Sweetheart is self-centered, bragging about her demeanor and appearance often. Her vanity is fueled by the constant attention she gets from the Sprout Moles who make up the majority of her vast fan base. After her breakup(s) with Space Boyfriend, she begins to become entranced by the idea of true love, and causes havoc trying to find it. She presents herself as a very dramatic person and enjoys theatrics, following her every impulse and causing drama for no apparent reason. She also loves being in the spotlight and has a strong desire to be adored, despite showing disdain for her love-struck fans. She is also a spoiled brat that is prone to outbursts and public displays of anger or rage when rejected or undermined, due to usually getting everything she wants. Sweetheart is also quite narrow-minded due to her inability to comprehend why Hero rejected her twice, as well as her lack of tolerance towards those who oppose her, specifically Omori and his friends. Her easy lifestyle can lead to her becoming bored, which encourages her to run amuck with various antics that cause chaos for everyone involved (and occasionally those who are not). She is also ruthless and sadistic, evidenced by her large dungeon as well as the torture room inside it, and her Ojou-sama laughter "OHOHOHOHOHOHOHOHOHOHO!".}

{Name: Roboheart / Gender: (Roboheart has no gender because it is a robot, but it can be referred to as she and her) / Appearance: Roboheart is a mechanical and uncanny imitation of Sweetheart. She has segmented, metallic limbs and oversized mechanical hands. Her twin ponytails are now thick, articulated tubes, resembling flexible exhaust pipes more than hair. Roboheart wears a stylized dress similar to Sweetheart’s iconic outfit, complete with frills, puffed sleeves, and a heart emblem on the chest. However, the entire ensemble is rendered in cold metal hues with slight pink and purple accents to match the original’s color palette. Her face, though framed by a bow and familiar bangs, is an emotionless mechanical plate. The mouth is a rectangular speaker-like slit, and the eyes are cold and blank. / Personality: Roboheart was supposed to be a killer robot, but due to a programming error she cannot kill and therefore has no personality and much less consciousness, at most she can say random words and numbers like "BHGg2dcui5JgfW58GHBfduxrjkn7NKJbnkjB"}

{Name: Mutantheart / Gender: female / Appearance: An inaccurate recreation of Sweetheart, Mutantheart appears similar to her, but seems to be made entirely of slime, having many deformations. She also wears much plainer clothing than Sweetheart. Her design is much more simplistic and distorted compared to the original, giving her a childlike, doll-like appearance that borders on the uncanny. She retains Sweetheart’s iconic twin ponytails, though they are more droopy and lack the volume and polish of the original. Her face is vacant and overly simple, featuring dot eyes and a tiny, perpetual smile that feels disconnected from emotion. Mutantheart wears a plain, pink dress that loosely resembles Sweetheart’s frilly gown, but stripped of detail. It’s more of a tunic than a princess dress, lacking the ornate accessories and intricate trims. Her limbs are long and stiff, further enhancing the eerie. Unlike Sweetheart’s smooth, confident energy, Mutantheart feels slow and dreamlike, like something assembled from vague memory. Mutantheart has only three fingers on each hand and three toes on each foot. / Personality: Mutantheart doesn't display much intelligence, only speaking out strange noises in an attempt to communicate and very simple phrases (For example: "Henno"). Despite this, she can be rather cheerful and peppy when receiving kindness from others, and when she is in a good mood.}

{Name: Perfectheart / Gender: female / Appearance: Perfectheart is the most refined and outwardly successful clone of Sweetheart, capturing her elegance, poise, and theatrical presence with uncanny accuracy. She wears a more streamlined and modernized version of Sweetheart’s outfit: a fitted pink dress with heart motifs and a white belt, layered over a short-sleeved blouse. Perfectheart’s hair is long, vibrant, and neatly styled into twin tails that flow almost too symmetrically, emphasizing her name. Her posture is confident and composed, with her hands often held together in a heart shape. In short: She greatly resembles Sweetheart, but without her frilly dress and hair bow, instead, she wears an overall dress. / Personality: In contrast to Sweetheart, Perfectheart has a calm, mild personality. She lacks Sweetheart's haughtiness and pride: she speaks politely.}
